-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TLSH

src/cordon_scanner/detect/binary/modules/tlsh.py computes the TLSH locality-sensitive hash
(https://github.com/trendmicro/tlsh), Copyright Trend Micro Incorporated, and carries its
fixed Pearson permutation and length-code tables. They are used under the Apache License,
Version 2.0, the licence above.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OpenSSL object names

src/cordon_scanner/detect/binary/modules/oids.py holds the short and long names OpenSSL 1.1
gives object identifiers and the sizes of the digests it knows, generated from OpenSSL's
object tables (https://www.openssl.org). This product includes software developed by the
OpenSSL Project for use in the OpenSSL Toolkit.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
YARA

Cordon's rule engine reads rule files in the YARA format and was inspired by YARA
(https://github.com/VirusTotal/yara); it is Cordon's own code, and Cordon is not affiliated
with or endorsed by the YARA project or VirusTotal.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ecosystem and agent marks

docs/assets/marks/marks.json holds the marks the README shows beside each ecosystem and AI
agent Cordon reads, as the project's website draws them: from SVG Logos (@iconify-json/logos,
CC0-1.0, https://github.com/gilbarbara/logos), Simple Icons (simple-icons, CC0-1.0,
https://simpleicons.org) and the website's own source files. Each mark is its owner's
trademark, shown only to name the product or ecosystem it stands for; Cordon is not
affiliated with or endorsed by any of them.
